{"text": "ESTATE OF BERNADETTE LOUISE KOWALCZYK, DECEASED\nWayne County Probate Court, File No. 2026-871442-DE\nInventory working notes (for Form PC 577) -- prepared by FA, 3/30/2026\n\nDecedent: Bernadette Louise Kowalczyk, d. February 3, 2026 at\nage 94. Born 9 June 1931 in Hamtramck. SSN on death cert:\nxxx-xx-7388. Widow of Stanislaw Kowalczyk (d. 2009). No children.\nPersonal rep: her nephew Casimir Kowalczyk (\"Caz\"),\nLetters of Authority issued 3/12/2026. Caz's cell: 313 555 0176.\nEstate EIN (applied online 3/16/2026): 92-3310847.\n\nREAL PROPERTY\n1. House at 88 Lindenwood Terrace, Dearborn, MI 48124.\n   Tax ID parcel 82-09-214-031. SEV x2 suggests about $212,000;\n   Caz got a realtor opinion of $235k. No mortgage. Appraisal\n   ordered.\n\nBANK / INVESTMENT\n2. Rouge River Community Credit Union -- share draft acct ending 4409,\n   date-of-death balance $14,882.19.\n3. RRCCU 18-month certificate no. 70041882 -- $50,000.00 plus\n   accrued int. $611.42. POD beneficiary named: Georgia Kowalczyk-Reed\n   (grand-niece). NON-PROBATE, list for info only.\n4. Penhallow & Strand Securities brokerage acct PSS-448-207716, DOD value\n   $386,240.77. Statement shows routing 043993190 for the sweep acct.\n   Penhallow needs a medallion signature + certified Letters to retitle to\n   \"Estate of Bernadette L. Kowalczyk\".\n\nVEHICLES / OTHER TITLED\n5. 2008 Buick Lucerne, VIN 1G4HD57258U164229, MI plate DWK 3391. KBB approx $3,100.\n6. 1987 Chris-Craft 26' cabin cruiser \"Polish Princess\", hull ID CCHEV187M87A,\n   kept at Lakeshore Marine Storage Co., St. Clair Shores. Storage arrears\n   $1,940 -- Lakeshore is asserting a lien.\n\nHOUSEHOLD / PERSONAL\n7. Furnishings, est. $4,000. Jewelry in safe deposit box #217 at RRCCU\n   Michigan Ave branch -- not yet opened, need Caz + credit union officer.\n8. Uncashed pension check, $1,206.00.\n\nDEBTS / CLAIMS SO FAR\n- Beaumont Hills Hospice final invoice $2,317.50 (decedent had advanced dementia\n  and congestive heart failure; on hospice from Nov.)\n- Funeral, paid by Caz personally: $9,480 -- reimburse as priority claim (MCL 700.3706? check).\n\nWILL (dated 10/14/2014, drafted by Hunter Dombrowski of\nDombrowski Law, P.C., bar no. P48113):\n- $25,000 to St. Hedwig Parish \"for Masses for my soul and Stan's\"\n- $10,000 to Georgia\n- residue to Caz.\nCaz says Hunter retired; original will was in the firm's vault and\nhas been filed. Georgia lives out of state and has asked for a copy --\nok to send per Ms. Abdullahi.\n\nOpen items: Form 706 not required (well under exemption). Confirm whether the 1099-R\npension payer needs the estate EIN. Next review with Faith Abdullahi on 4/9/2026.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "397 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Bernadette Louise Kowalczyk", "Stanislaw Kowalczyk", "Casimir Kowalczyk", "Georgia Kowalczyk-Reed", "Beaumont Hills", "Hunter Dombrowski", "Caz", "Faith Abdullahi", "Stan"], "companies": ["Wayne County Probate Court", "Rouge River Community Credit Union", "RRCCU", "Penhallow & Strand Securities", "Lakeshore Marine Storage Co.", "Beaumont Hills Hospice", "St. Hedwig Parish", "Dombrowski Law", "Georgia"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Hamtramck", "Dearborn", "Beverly Hills", "St. Clair Shores", "St. Hedwig Parish", "Georgia"], "health": ["dementia", "congestive heart failure"], "sensitive": [], "names": ["Bernadette Louise Kowalczyk", "Stanislaw Kowalczyk", "Casimir Kowalczyk", "Georgia Kowalczyk-Reed", "Hunter", "Stan", "Caz", "Faith", "Abdullahi"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region